gn","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fsign-in-design","03.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F04.sign-in-design",{"title":254,"path":255,"stem":256,"icon":257},"Development Server","\u002Fplatform\u002Fdevelopment-server","03.platform\u002F13.development-server","i-lucide-server-cog",{"title":259,"path":260,"stem":261,"icon":262},"Supply Chain Security","\u002Fplatform\u002Fsupply-chain-security","03.platform\u002F14.supply-chain-security","i-lucide-package-check",{"title":264,"path":265,"stem":266,"icon":267},"Enterprise License","\u002Fplatform\u002Fenterprise-license","03.platform\u002F15.enterprise-license","i-lucide-badge-check",{"id":269,"title":180,"body":270,"description":594,"extension":595,"links":596,"meta":597,"navigation":598,"path":181,"seo":599,"stem":182,"__hash__":600},"docs\u002F03.platform\u002F01.architecture.md",{"type":271,"value":272,"toc":585},"minimark",[273,277,281,285,349,357,361,429,433,436,446,452,457,468,513,519,523,545,578,581],[274,275,31],"h2",{"id":276},"overview",[278,279,280],"p",{},"Kinotic OS is a full-stack application platform that handles service communication, persistence, authentication, authorization, deployment, and observability. The system is composed of several core components that work together to provide a seamless development and runtime experience.",[274,282,284],{"id":283},"core-components","Core Components",[286,287,288,305,318,331,337,343],"ul",{},[289,290,291,295,296,300,301,304],"li",{},[292,293,294],"strong",{},"Management server"," (",[297,298,299],"code",{},"kinotic-server-management",") — The API the portal, the Kinotic CLI and organization members' MCP hosts call: sign-up, logins and invitations, the ",[297,302,303],{},"management-api"," services, and the GitHub App's webhook.",[289,306,307,295,310,313,314,317],{},[292,308,309],{},"System server",[297,311,312],{},"kinotic-server-system",") — The API the system console and the vm-managers call: the ",[297,315,316],{},"system-api"," services, project deployments, and the cluster singletons that reconcile deployments and delete old workload runs.",[289,319,320,295,323,326,327,330],{},[292,321,322],{},"App server",[297,324,325],{},"kinotic-server-app",") — The API every application's users, UIs and microservices call: the ",[297,328,329],{},"app-api"," persistence services and the services applications publish in their own zones, each application at its own API host.",[289,332,333,336],{},[292,334,335],{},"RPC Gateway"," — Each server's gateway routes remote procedure calls between its clients and published services over STOMP\u002FWebSocket, and serves the server's REST and MCP endpoints.",[289,338,339,342],{},[292,340,341],{},"Persistence Layer"," — Provides automatic CRUD operations for entities backed by Elasticsearch.",[289,344,345,348],{},[292,346,347],{},"Auth System"," — Handles authentication (email\u002Fpassword and OIDC) across three authorization hierarchies: System, Organization, and Application. Each server admits only the participants it serves.",[278,350,351,352,356],{},"The three servers are Spring Boot applications that form one Ignite cluster, in which each hosts only its own zones. ",[353,354,203],"a",{"href":355},"\u002Fplatform\u002Fdefense-in-depth#network-architecture"," shows which participants each admits and which zones each hosts.",[274,358,360],{"id":359},"tech-stack","Tech Stack",[362,363,364,377],"table",{},[365,366,367],"thead",{},[368,369,370,374],"tr",{},[371,372,373],"th",{},"Component",[371,375,376],{},"Technology",[378,379,380,389,397,405,413,421],"tbody",{},[368,381,382,386],{},[383,384,385],"td",{},"Orchestration",[383,387,388],{},"Kubernetes",[368,390,391,394],{},[383,392,393],{},"Build Isolation",[383,395,396],{},"Firecracker VMs",[368,398,399,402],{},[383,400,401],{},"Runtime",[383,403,404],{},"Bun",[368,406,407,410],{},[383,408,409],{},"Search\u002FPersistence",[383,411,412],{},"Elasticsearch",[368,414,415,418],{},[383,416,417],{},"Logging",[383,419,420],{},"Grafana Loki",[368,422,423,426],{},[383,424,425],{},"Payments",[383,427,428],{},"Stripe Connect",[274,430,432],{"id":431},"communication","Communication",[278,434,435],{},"Services communicate via STOMP over WebSocket, with messages routed by CRI (Kinotic Resource Identifier). Each service, method, and event stream is addressable through a CRI, which follows the format:",[437,438,443],"pre",{"className":439,"code":441,"language":442},[440],"language-text","scheme:\u002F\u002F[scope@]resourceName[\u002Fpath][#version]\n","text",[297,444,441],{"__ignoreMap":445},"",[278,447,448,449,451],{},"The RPC gateway uses CRIs to route requests to the correct service instance, apply versioning, and enforce scope-based multi-tenancy. See the ",[353,450,236],{"href":237}," reference for details.",[453,454,456],"h3",{"id":455},"kinotic-rpc-on-its-own","Kinotic RPC on its own",[278,458,459,460,463,464,467],{},"Kinotic RPC, the service and event layer in ",[297,461,462],{},"kinotic-core"," and ",[297,465,466],{},"kinotic-api-gateway",", runs without the rest of\nKinotic OS. A server built on it alone supplies two beans the gateway authenticates and authorizes every\nconnection with:",[362,469,470,480],{},[365,471,472],{},[368,473,474,477],{},[371,475,476],{},"Bean",[371,478,479],{},"What it decides",[378,481,482,495],{},[368,483,484,489],{},[383,485,486],{},[297,487,488],{},"SecurityService",[383,490,491,492],{},"Who a connection is: it authenticates the STOMP CONNECT headers and returns the connection's ",[297,493,494],{},"Participant",[368,496,497,502],{},[383,498,499],{},[297,500,501],{},"ZoneRulesResolver",[383,503,504,505,508,509,512],{},"What that participant may address: the ",[297,506,507],{},"ZoneRules"," of zones it may send to and subscribe in, which the gateway narrows to the zones the server's ",[297,510,511],{},"ZonePartitioningService"," serves",[278,514,515,516,518],{},"Kinotic OS's servers supply each from their own module: the ",[297,517,488],{}," of the server, and kinotic-domain's\nresolver, which gives system, organization and application participants their zones.",[453,520,522],{"id":521},"never-block-the-event-loop","Never block the event loop",[278,524,525,526,529,530,533,534,533,537,540,541,544],{},"A Java service published with ",[297,527,528],{},"@Publish"," is invoked on a Vert.x event loop it shares with the other services on the node, the same rule Vert.x sets for its own handlers. A method returns a ",[297,531,532],{},"Future",", ",[297,535,536],{},"CompletableFuture",[297,538,539],{},"Mono"," or ",[297,542,543],{},"Flux"," and lets the work complete off the loop; a method that is slow, because it blocks on a synchronous client, a lock or a sleep, or because it does heavy CPU work, hands that work off inside itself:",[437,546,550],{"className":547,"code":548,"language":549,"meta":445,"style":445},"language-java shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","@Override\npublic Future\u003CReport> render(String id) {\n    return vertx.executeBlocking(() -> renderer.render(id));   \u002F\u002F the loop is free while the worker runs\n}\n","java",[297,551,552,560,566,572],{"__ignoreMap":445},[553,554,557],"span",{"class":555,"line":556},"line",1,[553,558,559],{},"@Override\n",[553,561,563],{"class":555,"line":562},2,[553,564,565],{},"public Future\u003CReport> render(String id) {\n",[553,567,569],{"class":555,"line":568},3,[553,570,571],{},"    return vertx.executeBlocking(() -> renderer.render(id));   \u002F\u002F the loop is free while the worker runs\n",[553,573,575],{"class":555,"line":574},4,[553,576,577],{},"}\n",[278,579,580],{},"The platform never hands off on a service's behalf. A method that blocks stalls every service sharing its loop, and Vert.x's blocked-thread checker reports it in the log.",[582,583,584],"style",{},"html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-dark);background: var(--shiki-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-dark-text-decoration);}html.dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-dark);background: var(--shiki-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-dark-text-decoration);}",{"title":445,"searchDepth":562,"depth":562,"links":586},[587,588,589,590],{"id":276,"depth":562,"text":31},{"id":283,"depth":562,"text":284},{"id":359,"depth":562,"text":360},{"id":431,"depth":562,"text":432,"children":591},[592,593],{"id":455,"depth":568,"text":456},{"id":521,"depth":568,"text":522},"High-level architecture of the Kinotic OS platform.","md",null,{},{"icon":183},{"title":180,"description":594},"XDYJHkUIXJgggly1Ml1BDSFbO1_1sW2E-a8E5kAfKNU",[602,604],{"title":171,"path":172,"stem":173,"description":603,"icon":94,"children":-1},"Complete SQL grammar reference for migration scripts.",{"title":185,"path":186,"stem":187,"description":605,"icon":6,"children":-1},"Deploying and operating Kinotic OS in various environments.",1792930936789]